  "body": "Tucked away on an expansive, tree-lined site just a five-minute stroll from the waterfront, this charming, freestanding 1930s weatherboard residence offers the ultimate St Heliers lifestyle. Spanning an impressive 280 sq m (approx) over two thoughtfully designed levels, it delivers a practical, family-friendly layout packed with character and future potential.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the home, light-filled open-plan living and kitchen areas flow effortlessly into a separate lounge and dining space. Step out onto sunlit entertaining decks to relax and take in views across lush gardens toward St Heliers Beach and Vellenoweth Green.\r\n\r\nOutside, your private outdoor retreat awaits - complete with a spa pool, fire pit and mature trees illuminated by timed feature lights. Native tui and fantails are daily visitors, creating a peaceful, resort-like atmosphere right at home.\r\n\r\nThe upper level accommodates four spacious bedrooms and two bathrooms, the lower boasts a generous multipurpose room, currently set up as an office, gym, and music space with extensive storage to suit your lifestyle. Parking is exceptionally generous, featuring a single garage plus two extended double carports and a third parking bay, offering ample space for multiple cars, guests, or a boat.\r\n\r\nThe current owners have drafted future renovation plans (available to view at open homes).  Also potential to build up and further maximize the stunning sea views.\r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned within an easy stroll of the beach, village, cafés, tennis/bowling clubs, and local amenities, and zoned for prestigious schools: Glendowie College, St Heliers School, and St Ignatius.\r\n\r\nProperties of this calibre in St Heliers are rarely available. Visit the upcoming open homes or contact me to arrange your private viewing.\r\n\r\nAuction:  12:00p.m. Monday 23rd November.  In Rooms:  393 Tamaki Drive, St Heliers (unless sold prior).",
